---
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs10.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Part of the DRS consolidation wave" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Why withdrawn" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="withdrawn"
    explanation="This standard has been withdrawn."
    targetStatus="Replaced by DRS 18"
    link="/germany/drs/drs18"
    linkText="View DRS 18"
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Part of the DRS consolidation wave</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">Part of the DRS consolidation wave</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 10 elaborated the deferred-tax mechanics for group accounts specifically, supplementing the general HGB deferred-tax framework (§274, established in the earlier HGB poster series) alongside the additional consolidation-specific temporary differences §306 HGB creates — the extra layer of deferred tax arising from consolidation adjustments themselves (such as eliminated intragroup profit) sitting on top of each entity's own individual deferred-tax position.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Why withdrawn — a straightforward renumbering into the current cluster</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">Why withdrawn — a straightforward renumbering into the current cluster</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 10 was superseded by DRS 18 "Latente Steuern," which remains the CURRENT, active standard on this topic — itself amended as recently as 2021 (DRÄS 11) to tighten its alignment with the current statutory text and remove certain disclosure requirements that had gone beyond the legal minimum. DRS 18 sits slightly outside the main 22–27 modernisation cluster numerically, but is very much part of the same broader wave of standards actively maintained today.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topic</span><span>Deferred taxes in group accounts, including consolidation-specific temporary differences</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Successor</span><span><strong>DRS 18 — Latente Steuern</strong> (current, active — see the DRS 18 poster for full detail)</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
